# pi-bridge

## Intent
Keep Effect execution and failure mapping at the Pi boundary so policy cores remain Pi-free.

## Contract
Input: an Effect program and optional Pi abort signal.
Output: the program value, a fail-closed handler decision, or a Pi tool result.
Errors: typed Git, GitLab, and repository-policy lookup failures become readable blocking reasons; defects, unexpected failures, and interruption also fail closed.

## Behaviour
Run the Effect program with the supplied abort signal.
Return successful values unchanged.
Map typed failures, defects, unexpected failures, and interruption to safe Pi-facing results.

## Edge cases
- The abort signal interrupts verification -> return an actionable retry reason.
- A typed lookup fails -> identify the unavailable subsystem in the blocking reason.
- A defect or unknown thrown value occurs -> block without rejecting the Pi handler promise.

## Non-goals
This module does not implement policy decisions or register Pi extensions.

## Evidence
Pi handlers are Promise-based while harness modules use Effect error channels and interruption.